    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n20220" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">βοηθ-ητικός</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ή</span>,
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">όν</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>ready</i> or <i>able to help, serviceable</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τιϝί</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Arist.
					<u>Rh.</u>
					1374a24
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τοῖς πένησι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plu.
					<u>Sol.</u>
					29
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τῶν δεομένων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Diotog.
				</span></i>
			 ap. <i><span class="en">
				Stob.
				4.7.62
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πρός τι</span> so as to <i>keep
				it off</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>Pol.</u>
				1267a16
			</span></i>; or towards <i>promoting it</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>HA</u>
				515b9
			</span></i>: 
				Comp.
			
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-ώτερον, τὸ ἄρρεν τοῦ θήλεος</span>
			ib. <i><span class="en">
				608b15
			</span></i>: 
				Sup.
			
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-ώτατος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Iamb.
					<u>VP</u>
					25.111
				</span></i>
			.</div>
